     "y": 575,
     "title": "Picture element",
     "text": "The word pixel is short for 'picture element'. Your phone's camera captures tens of millions of them at once."
    },
    {
     "id": "f2",
     "face": "right",
     "x": 1888,
     "y": 540,
     "title": "True colour",
     "text": "24-bit colour uses 8 bits each for red, green and blue, giving 16.7 million shades: more than the human eye can distinguish."
    },
    {
     "id": "f3",
     "face": "back",
     "x": 880,
     "y": 609,
     "title": "Why images look blocky",
     "text": "Enlarging a bitmap doesn't add detail, so pixels become visible. Vector images, drawn from shapes, don't have that problem."
    },
    {
     "id": "f4",
     "face": "back",
     "x": 1888,
     "y": 540,
     "title": "Hidden GPS",
